From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: include the MDE in EAPOL-Key msg 3/4 for a non-AP MLD

For a non-AP MLD the authenticator does not copy the common
RSNE/RSNXE/MDE block (wpa_ie) into EAPOL-Key msg 3/4; each affiliated
link's RSNE and RSNXE are delivered in its MLO Link KDE instead. With an
FT AKM this silently dropped the Mobility Domain element from the Key
Data, while the FTE was still added. IEEE Std 802.11 12.7.6.4 requires
the MDE at the top level of msg 3/4 for an FT initial mobility domain
association, and wpa_supplicant's MLO path (ft_validate_mdie) rejects
msg 3/4 when it is missing; a Qualcomm-based non-AP MLD answered every
msg 3/4 with an unprotected Disassociate for the same reason.

Write the MDE into the Key Data before the FTE when the STA is a
non-AP MLD. The existing FT length reservation already covers it.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
@@ -5290,6 +5290,25 @@
 	if (wpa_key_mgmt_ft(sm->wpa_key_mgmt)) {
 		int res;
 
+		if (is_mld) {
+			/*
+			 * The common RSNE/RSNXE/MDE block (wpa_ie) is not copied
+			 * into EAPOL-Key msg 3/4 for a non-AP MLD (each link's
+			 * RSNE/RSNXE travels in its MLO Link KDE instead), but
+			 * the MDE is still required at the top level of the Key
+			 * Data (IEEE Std 802.11 12.7.6.4): the non-AP MLD checks
+			 * it against the (Re)Association Response MDE before it
+			 * accepts the FTE, and rejects msg 3/4 when it is absent.
+			 */
+			res = wpa_write_mdie(conf, pos, kde + kde_len - pos);
+			if (res < 0) {
+				wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
+					   "FT: Failed to insert MDE into EAPOL-Key Key Data");
+				goto done;
+			}
+			pos += res;
+		}
+
 		if (sm->assoc_resp_ftie &&
 		    kde + kde_len - pos >= 2 + sm->assoc_resp_ftie[1]) {
 			os_memcpy(pos, sm->assoc_resp_ftie,
